    "83691951b0": {
      "id": "83691951b0",
      "created": 1795259393.700483,
      "headline": "Roglič to get a new coach for the first time as a pro",
      "url": "https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/teams-riders/maybe-this-will-add-something-more-primoz-roglic-will-change-coach-for-the-first-time-in-his-career-following-move-to-nsn/",
      "source": "Cyclingnews",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259391/cycling-bot/83691951b0-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259391/cycling-bot/83691951b0-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259392/cycling-bot/83691951b0-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259392/cycling-bot/83691951b0-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795259393/cycling-bot/83691951b0-3.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Primož Roglič is set to work with a new coach for the first time in his career.\n\nCyclingnews understands that long-time coach Marc Lamberts will not follow him to NSN Cycling. Slovenia's national coach Uroš Murn points to Tadej Pogačar's coaching switch as a sign that a change can help. NSN has not yet said who will coach Roglič in 2027.\n\nCan a new coach bring something extra from Roglič at 37?\n\nSource: Cyclingnews\n\n#cycling #procycling #roadcycling #WorldTour #PrimozRoglic #Roglic #NSNCycling #RedBullBora #cyclingnews #cyclingtransfers",
      "alt_text": "News graphic with the headline that Primož Roglič will have a new coach for the first time in his professional career after joining NSN Cycling.",
      "score": 7,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "RIDER NEWS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "Lamberts stays at Red Bull",
          "text": "Cyclingnews understands Marc Lamberts will not follow Primož Roglič to NSN Cycling. He is set to remain on the coaching staff at Red Bull-Bora-Hansgrohe in 2027."
        },
        {
          "title": "A partnership since 2016",
          "text": "Lamberts has coached Roglič since he turned pro with LottoNL-Jumbo in 2016, and moved with him to Red Bull in 2024. Roglič, 37, joins NSN on a one-year contract."
        },
        {
          "title": "The Pogačar example",
          "text": "Slovenia coach Uroš Murn cited Pogačar's 2024 switch from Iñigo San Millán to Javier Sola, saying Roglič has nothing to lose. NSN has not confirmed who will coach him in 2027."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 213
    },
    "9760f965bd": {
      "id": "9760f965bd",
      "created": 1795262939.7114208,
      "headline": "Tour du Rwanda unveils new format with two classic races",
      "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5",
      "source": "The New Times",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795262939/cycling-bot/9760f965bd-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795262939/cycling-bot/9760f965bd-0.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Tour du Rwanda is changing its format.\n\nOrganisers have announced a new-look event that brings two classic races into the programme, according to The New Times. The report's headline is all we have so far, so details on the races, dates and how the new structure will work are still to come.\n\nWe'll update when the full programme is published.\n\nWhat would you like to see from a reworked Tour du Rwanda?\n\nSource: The New Times\n\n#TourduRwanda #Cycling #ProCycling #RoadCycling #CyclingNews #UCIAfricaTour #AfricanCycling #Rwanda #RaceAnnouncement #RoadRacing",
      "alt_text": "Graphic with the text 'Tour du Rwanda unveils new format with two classic races' under a Race News label.",
      "score": 5,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "RACE NEWS",
      "slides": [],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 216
    },
    "d77264a216": {
      "id": "d77264a216",
      "created": 1795266553.0175931,
      "headline": "Pogačar wants Paris-Roubaix back on his 2027 calendar",
      "url": "https://escapecollective.com/no-big-secret-pogacar-also-targets-paris-roubaix-in-busy-2027/",
      "source": "Escape Collective",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795266531/cycling-bot/d77264a216-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795266531/cycling-bot/d77264a216-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795266532/cycling-bot/d77264a216-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795266532/cycling-bot/d77264a216-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795266533/cycling-bot/d77264a216-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795266534/cycling-bot/d77264a216-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Tadej Pogačar has said he wants to ride Paris-Roubaix again in 2027.\n\nSpeaking to Sporza, the Slovenian called his interest \"no big secret\" and said he wants another near-perfect season first. He has finished second in both of his Roubaix starts so far. A win would give him all five Monuments, following his Milan-San Remo victory earlier in 2026.\n\nCan he finally beat the cobbles in 2027? 🚴\n\nSource: Escape Collective\n\n#Pogacar #TadejPogacar #ParisRoubaix #UAETeamEmirates #Cycling #ProCycling #RoadCycling #CobbledClassics #Monuments #WorldTour",
      "alt_text": "News graphic with the headline that Tadej Pogačar wants to return to Paris-Roubaix in 2027.",
      "score": 9,
      "reel_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/video/upload/v1795266552/cycling-bot/d77264a216-reel.mp4",
      "category": "RIDER NEWS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "Pogačar eyes Roubaix in 2027",
          "text": "Tadej Pogačar told Sporza he would like to compete at Paris-Roubaix again in 2027. He said it is \"no big secret\" and that he wants the whole season to be perfect first."
        },
        {
          "title": "Two starts, two second places",
          "text": "Roubaix has so far gone to others. Pogačar was second behind Mathieu van der Poel, despite a late crash, and then second behind Wout van Aert after a two-up sprint in the velodrome."
        },
        {
          "title": "The rest of his 2027 plans",
          "text": "He has said he will again build his season around the Tour de France. The Haute-Savoie world title and a return to the Vuelta are also priorities, and the UAE Tour has been suggested as his opener."
        },
        {
          "title": "Why it matters",
          "text": "Victory at Roubaix would complete his set of Monuments, following his Milan-San Remo win earlier in 2026."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 223
    },
    "0116f42edb": {
      "id": "0116f42edb",
      "created": 1795327741.1338015,
      "headline": "Harper and Storer confirmed for 2027 Tour Down Under",
      "url": "https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/teams-riders/tour-down-under-adds-australian-chris-harper-and-michael-storer-to-2027-lineup/",
      "source": "Cyclingnews",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795327738/cycling-bot/0116f42edb-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795327738/cycling-bot/0116f42edb-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795327739/cycling-bot/0116f42edb-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795327739/cycling-bot/0116f42edb-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795327740/cycling-bot/0116f42edb-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795327740/cycling-bot/0116f42edb-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "Two Australian riders and their teams are confirmed for the 2027 Tour Down Under.\n\nChris Harper will lead Pinarello Q36.5 on its race debut, while Michael Storer returns with Tudor. The WorldTour opener starts on January 19 and covers 874km over six days.\n\nWhich Australian are you backing to shine on home roads?\n\nSource: Cyclingnews\n\n#TourDownUnder #TDU2027 #WorldTour #ProCycling #RoadCycling #ChrisHarper #MichaelStorer #PinarelloQ365 #TudorProCycling #Cycling",
      "alt_text": "News graphic announcing that Chris Harper and Michael Storer will ride the 2027 Tour Down Under with Pinarello Q36.5 and Tudor.",
      "score": 7,
      "reel_url": null,
      "category": "RACE NEWS",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "Two more Australians confirmed",
          "text": "The 2027 Tour Down Under has added Chris Harper and Michael Storer to its lineup, along with their ProTeams, Pinarello Q36.5 and Tudor."
        },
        {
          "title": "Harper and Pinarello Q36.5 debut",
          "text": "Pinarello Q36.5 makes its first appearance at the race. Harper has ridden every edition since 2017, with 14th overall in 2025 his best. The final stage passes through Aldgate, where he grew up."
        },
        {
          "title": "Storer leads Tudor",
          "text": "Tudor returns for a second year with Storer, who last rode in 2024 and finished 20th with the Australian national team. Tudor's Marco Brenner was fourth in January, two seconds off the podium."
        },
        {
          "title": "Race details",
          "text": "Racing starts on January 19 and covers 874km over six days. Jai Hindley has also been announced and will make his first start at the race since 2023."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 239
    },
    "efcb56eb6d": {
      "id": "efcb56eb6d",
      "created": 1795327752.2782423,
      "headline": "Maryland Cycling Classic cancelled after five years",
